                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Another abomination dragged-and-dropped to life in the hideous GameGuru engine and spat out onto Steam like a lingering dangle of phlegm, [b]Alone K.W.[/b] barely has the decency to even launch, let alone provide any measure of appealing gameplay. \n\nThe first loading screen lasted nearly four minutes for me and has apparently taken longer for some if it forgoes crashing after ten seconds. The game itself granted me a few minutes of actual playtime before refusing to let me interact with a keypad to progress. The flashlight battery change similarly refused to play ball, leaving me to poke the 'Use' key to no avail in the darkness while the game occasionally reminded me of the controls for fruitlessly pushing scenery crates around.\n\nIsn't the point of GameGuru, an engine that mocks your attempts to implement your own scripts, that although any product that comes out of it will be an asset-drowned high school project at best, its sheer simplification of game creation is meant to be stable? This is about as solidly built as a gangrene sufferer and nowhere near as contagious.\n\nWhatever pitiful moments of my life were taken by this disgrace are documented below.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=35aT2vSuHkc",
